eng. - Karlos Code
-this an universal language created to translate different types of APT into G-Code and the other way around

-original use in Karlo Ugrins APT - Gcode project transfer of data between APT reader and G-code writer in JSON format
-all of the comands are single meaning making it very easy to both write in KC and read from KC
-every command written is saved as an independed string in the JSON
--So let's begin with defining the commands--


"$"
    -this sign is used to break a line into 2 lines
    -at the end of a row there can only be one $ sign, at the begining of next row there shall not be any $ sign

"COMMENT:This is a comment"
    -COMMENT is defining that this string is a comment (evidently)
    - ":" marks that this the end of command that was prevoiuslty stated
    - now begins the actual comment
    -THE COMMENT BEGINS IMMEDIATELY AFTER ":"
        -that way translating the comment is way easier and logic goes:
            -> if line contains "COMMENT" -> line replace "COMMENT:" with symbol for the comment (for example $, then we would have $This is a comment)
    -before ending the line with " there shall not any spaces or sings unless it is a part of the comment itself
    -There are NO other elements for this command
"COMMENT:This is an example for a comment " with comment sing in the output comment being "$" output will be "$This is an example for a comment " <- notice the space before " as that is the way Comand line ended

"ADD: add_info"
    -ADD defines a header of the G-code
    -add_info may contain RADIUS to define that the g code is written in radius values, or DIAMETER for diameter
    -add_info may be defined in other ways but MUST be used to define a g code command and in that case shall not contain RADIUS or DIAMETER

"UNIT: unit_type"
    -UNIT command shall define what measuremnt unit type is used
    -default units are milimeters
    -unit_type can be:
        MM - milimeters
        INCH - inches
        FT - feet
        M - meter
        YARD - yards
        CB - cable (1/10 of NM - 185.2 M)
        KM - kilometer
        LM - land mile
        NM - nautical mile - 1852 M
        LY - light year (I mean just to be sure we cover everything)
    -unit_type shall be distanced from ":" exactly 1 space
    -before ending the line with " there shall not be any spaces or 
    -There are NO other elements for this command
"UNIT: MM"
    0   1

"PLANE: plane"
    -defines the working plane
    -"plane" shall be defined as represented:
        -"xy" - for xy plane
        -"xz" - for xz plane
        -"zy" - for zy plane

"TOOL: tool_info"
    -TOOL defines what tool is being used 
    -tool_info shall begin exactly one space after ":"
    -tool_info shall be consisted of the following information:
    "tool_name"
        -tool_name may be a variable for example "Threading+tool+d15+b7" where the spaces are defined with "+"
        -if there is NO tool name defined tool_name shall be valued as "++" -> " NAME:++ "        
        -tool_name shall be spaced exactly 0 spaces from "NAME:"
    "slot_number"
        -slot_number may be a variable but shall only be a number
        -if there is NO slot number defined slot_number shall be valued as "++"
        -slot_number shall be represented as a 3 digit number beginning from 000, 001 untill 999
        -slot_number shall be spaced exactly 0 spaces from "MAGAZINE:"
    "tool_compensation"
        -tool_compensation may be a variable but shall only be a number
        -if there is NO tool compensation number defined tool_compensation shall be valued as "++"
        -tool_compensation shall be represented as a 3 digit number beginning from 000, 001 untill 999
        -tool_compensation shall be spaced exactly 0 spaces from "COMPENSAION:"
    "coolant_type"
        -coolant_type shall define what type of coolant is used by default for this tool
        -if there is no coolant coolant_type shall be defined with ++
        -if the coolant that isn't a default one is being used it must not be defiend only with "COOLANT: on"
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"TOOL: bean_cutter, 4, 67, flood"
    0       1      2  3    4

"SPINDLE: spindle_info"
    -this defines a change in spindle information
    -spindle_info shall consist of the following information:
        -current state of the spindle that is valued either as "on", "off" or "lock", !! in case of value="off/lock" the rest of spindle_info may be undefined exept for the spindle number
        -type of the spindle speed defining surface speed as "surface" and constant speed in revolutions as "fix", in case of state being "off" or "lock" it can be undefined
        -spindle speed and in case of state being "off" or "lock" it can be undefined
        -direction defining if the spindle is turning clockwise "cw" or counter clockwise "ccw"
    -if max limit for spindle speed is being set then spindle_infoshall consist of the following:
        -"MAX,value" where value is defining the maximum allowed spindle speed in RPM
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"SPINDLE: on, fix, 1500, cw, 1"
"SPINDLE:  off, 1"
"SPINDLE: MAX, 1500"
    0       1  2     3    4  5

"FEEDRATE: feedrate_info"
    -this defines the speed of changing tool position during "CUT"
    -feedrate_info shall consist of the following information:
        -type of feedrate defined eiter as "time" for -distance per minute- or "rev" for -distance per revolution- or "inver" for inverse feed type -> 1/"time"
        -speed of the feedrate defining it's value
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"FEEDRATE: rev, 0.05"
    0        1    2

"COOLANT: coolant_info"
    -in case of using a coolant that is a defaulted to the current tool the syntacs "COOLANT: STATE:on" is allowed
    -defines what type of coolant is used
    -coolant_info shall consist of the following information:
        -current state is valued either as "on" or "off", !! in case of value="off" the rest of coolant_info may be undefined
        -type of coolant valued either as "mist" for light fluid or "flood" for heavy fluid usage
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
    -in case of using coolant that was defined at the tool call  allowed sytacs is "COOLANT: on"
"COOLANT: on, flood"
"COOLANT: off"
    0       1   2

"AIR_PURGE: state"
    -defines usage of compressed air for clearing chips and simmilar usages
    -"state" is a variable defined either as "on" or "off"

"MOVEMENT: movement_type"
    -MOVEMENT defines that there is a change in the way next point is defined whether it is incremental movement or absolute movement
    -movement_type shall be spaced exactly 1 space from the "MOVEMENT:"
    -for Incremental, movement_type will be defined as "incremental"
    -for Absolute, movement_type will be defined as "absolute"

"AIR"
    -defines that next lines are executed in rapid movement meaning that the workpiece is not being cut 

"CUT"
    -defines that next lines are executed in cutting movement meaning that the workpiece is being cut 

"END"
    -defines that this is it. there is nothing more to be done, the program is finished

"ERROR"
    -defines that an error has occured
    -the form for this command may be flexible but the line must with EROR and any aditioan information must start 1 space after ERROR

"MULTAX: value"
    -value may only be on / off
    -value = on signals that this is a multi axial operation

"COMPENSATION_CHG:value"
    -this compenstation register has some changes that need to be logged
    -defines the compensation for the tool and consits of the following:
        "correction_register" it defines what corrector is being edited it can be valued from 1 to 99
        "cutter_quadrant" defines what point on cutter is being looked at
            -values are following: BR for (P4), BC for (P8), BL for (P3), CR for (P5), CC for (P9), CL for (P7), TR for (P1), TC for (P6), TL for (P2), and OFF
            -look at image.png in DOCUMENTATIONS
        "compensation_coords" it contains the X, Y, Z distance set
        "nose_radius" defines the radius on the tip of the cutting bit
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"COMPENSATION_CHG: 1, TC, 12, 34.5, 6, 0.7"
        0      1   2   3   4    5   6

"COMPENSATION_SET:value"
    -this tool takes a different compensation register
    -it must contain the tool number and new compensation register
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"COMPENSATION_SET: 3, 6"
   0               1  2

"CUTCOM:value"
    -cutting compensation
    -value can be: on off left right normds_on/off normps_on/off
    -I have no Idea what any of this is but its something from catia apt
    

"ROTHED: value"
    -defines the rotation of the tool head
    -value shall contain:
        -axis of rotation written either as x or y or z or i or j or K
        -type of rotation written as ABS or INC where ABS means the absolute axis angle and INC means an incremental angle
        -direction or rotation defining which way does the tool head move written as cw or ccw
        -angle defining the set angle
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"ROTHED: k, ABS, cw, 15"
    0    1  2   3  4

"ROTABL: value"
    - same as for "ROTHED" exept the first word what is changed to ROTABL

"MILL_TURRET_INVERSION"
    - this states that the turret is now inverted

"TLAXIS: value"
    -defines tool axies
    -value is a set of numerical varables that describe the direction of cutting motion in IJK vectors
    -the resultant vector must be equal to 1
    -TLAXIS definition is needed for axial machining like tapping, drilling, reaming
    -if the cutting motion is completed down the Z axis "TLAXIS: 0, 0, -1";
    -if it is up the Z axis K=1
    -if it is equaly on both z and x axis "TLAXIS: 0.7071, 0, -0.7071"

"LINE: X Y Z A B C"
    -LINE: means that there is a linear movement
    X
        -X shall contain "X" followed by a numerical value with undefined decimals both of positive and negative value
        -"X" shall be spaced exactly 1 space from the previous element
        -numerical value must have at least 1 whole number and 1 decimal number divided with a "."
        -if the numerical value is negative "-" sign must be present after "X" but before numerical value
        -in case of the x coordinate not changing the numerical value, it may be presented as "++"
        -inside the whole X there shall be no spaces
    Same aplies for all of the remeining elements but they must be ordered in the following array X Y Z A B C
    In case of not using multi axial machining process the ABC element may be left out
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"LINE: X10, Y++, Z30, A24, B35, C++"
"LINE: X10, Y34, Z++"
    0   1    2    3    4    5    6

"DWELL: dwell_info"
    -defines how long the tool is dwelling/stopped whilst the spindle is spinning
    -dwell_info must consist of the following information:
        -type to wait that is valued either as "rev" meaning how many revolutions until next command or "time" for amount of time in seconds until next command
        -value defining how much of the given unist is the wait
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
"DWELL: time, 12"
    0     1   2

"ARCH/arch_info"
    -defines a partial cicular movement 
    -this movement can only be performed in one of the 3 base planes given in "PLANE: value"
    -arch_info must consist of the following information:
        "CETER, value" containg XYZ component of the circle center
        "AXIS, value" defining circle axis component
        "TANGENT, value" defining a vector tangent to the begining of the circle
        "INFO, value" defining it's radius, direction and angle
        "END, value" defining it's end coordinates
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
        Values: (X)(Y)(Z)(I)(J)(K) shall not be in final output
"ARCH/CENTER, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30
ARCH/AXIS, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0
ARCH/TANGENT, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0
ARCH/INFO, 12, cw, angle
ARCH/END, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30"

"SINUS/sinus_info"
    -defines that the movement to the end point is a part of SINUS wave or multiple waves 
    -this movement can only be performed in one of the 3 base planes given in "PLANE: value"
    -sinus_info must consist of the following information:
        "CENTER, vlaue" defining the begining point of the sinusoidal midline
        "AXIS, value" deining the direction of the midline
        "TANGENT, value" defining the vector tangent to the beginning point of the sinusoide
        "INFO, value" consisting of the AMPLITUDE
        "END, value" consisting of the final coordinates
    -each element must be separated with one comma (,) and at least one space from the other elements
        Values: (X)(Y)(Z)(I)(J)(K) shall not be in final output
"SINUS/CENTER, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30
SINUS/AXIS, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0
SINUS/TANGENT, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0
SINUS/INFO, 12
SINUS/END, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30"

"HELIX/helix_info"
    -defines a spiral movement
    -helix_info must consist of the following information
        -"CENTER, value" where value is a numerical variable defining coordinates of top-most center point of the spiral path
        -"TANGENT, value" where value is a numerical variable defining a vector tangent to the first point on path looking from the top (- not counting the pitch)
        -"AXIS, value" where value is a numerical variable defining a vector paralel to the center of the spiral
        -"INFO, value" where value defines helix pitch, helix radius, helix height, helix full turns
        -"END: value" where value is a numerical variable defining the end point of the spiral
        Values: (X)(Y)(Z)(I)(J)(K) shall not be in final output
        -each element mus be separated with one comma and at least one space
        -this is how the final output must look like
"HELIX/CENTER, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30 
HELIX/TANGENT, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0 
HELIX/AXIS, (I)0.707, (J)-0.707, (K)0 
HELIX/INFO, 1.5 11.5 30 19 
HELIX/END, (X)10, (Y)20, (Z)30"

Cycles
One cycle must be defined like following:
"CYCLE/NAME cycle_name"

"CYCLE/DATA, cycle_data"
    -defines the  basic data about this cycle
    -the correct direction of spindle rotation must be previously defined
    -cycle_data shall consist of the following:
        total_depth which defines total distance that tool cuts the workpiece in cutting motion, after the approach clearance
        clearance which defines the distance from the tool tip to the workpiece surface
        feedrate_info that consists of feedrate value and unit (rev or time)
        spindle_info that consits of spindle value and unit (surface or fix)
        retract_type that defines if the retraction is rapid (1) or in specific feedrate (0)
        retract_feed defines the feedrate retraction if it isn't rapid
    -each element must be separated with 1 comma (,) and at lest one space from the previous element

"CYCLE/CYnum, CYnum_data"
    -for different cycles there are needed specific parameters
    CY0 -no aditional parameters
        -used for simple drilling where the tool does the cutting and returns

    CY1, dwell_mode, dwell_value
            -dwell_mode defines if it is set in time (2), revolutions (1) or if there is none (0)
            -dwell_value defines the waiting amount in given units

    CY2, dwell_mode, dwell_value, peck_size
            -where peck_size is the peck size
    
    CY3, dwell_mode, dwell_value, peck_size, decrement_rate, decrement_limit
            -decrement_rate defines the percentage of how much is the current peck smaller than the last one
            -decrement_limit defines the number the decrement rate is applied
    CY4, tool_pitch
            -used for single pass thread creating

"CYCLE/COORD"
    -contains the xyz component of the begining points of each cycle, clearance included
    -it mus be formated like following:
    -every set of coordinate must be separated with / 
    - and every coordinate separated with a comma from the other coordinate
"CYCLE/COORD/ 12, 34, 56 / 12, 34, 57/...

"CYCLE/DATA, cycle_data"
CYCLE/CY1, CY1_data"
CYCLE/COORD"

    
